  "description": "Identifies robots that pose a significant safety hazard based on their history of incidents, considering both absolute counts and incident rates.",
  "definition": "A robot is classified as 'High Safety-Risk' if it meets either of the following criteria: 1. It has experienced more than 5 total collisions. 2. Its combined rate of major incidents (collisions, zone violations, and speed violations) is greater than 2.0 per 1000 hours of operation."
}

